This is a working _non released_ stoopid, stoopid, stoopid, set 'o' doors
that do a CLS and print a banner, before doing each corresponding
function.  Allowed me to get away from the stock standard feel of MAXs user
settings, and thus make my menus more consistant.

Could be modified to accept passwords, etc, etc.

To compile the source, you'll need SAS C 6.X.

To install it, just use sumthin' akin to this:

  KEY  FUNCTION  EXTRAS  LOW  HIGH   PATH/FILENAME
   C      34       0     10   10000  DOORS:SETTINGS/<FILE>

Where <FILE> = ANSI, CLS, Computer, etc, etc.


